# Figma → Code Workflow

1. Call the Figma MCP `get_design_context` on the target node BEFORE writing any code.
2. Treat the generated code as a REFERENCE only — always translate it to the project's stack (framework + UI kit components).
3. Map design elements to existing kit/project components first. Fall back to custom markup only when nothing matches.
4. Icons/images: export as SVG first (see `svg-icon-components.mdc`) — Figma MCP asset URLs expire (~7 days). NEVER hand-write SVG paths or invent placeholder icons. Raster (PNG/WebP) into `static/assets/<feature>/` only for inherently bitmap assets.
5. Auto-layout maps to flex/grid utilities; keep spacing, radii and font sizes faithful to the design.
6. Hints priority: Code Connect > component docs > design annotations > design tokens > raw hex/absolute positioning.

## RTL Mirroring (critical for RTL apps)

The app is RTL (`dir="rtl"` on `<html>`), but generated Figma code is written with **LTR physical utilities** (`left-*`, `right-*`, `pl-*`, `pr-*`, `ml-*`, `mr-*`, `text-left`). Physical utilities do NOT flip in an RTL document, so using them verbatim places everything **mirrored** compared to the design. Always convert:

| Figma output               | Write instead (logical)   |
| -------------------------- | ------------------------- |
| `left-*` / `right-*`       | `inset-e-*` / `inset-s-*` |
| `pl-*` / `pr-*`            | `pe-*` / `ps-*`           |
| `ml-*` / `mr-*`            | `me-*` / `ms-*`           |
| `text-left` / `text-right` | `text-end` / `text-start` |

Additional mirroring rules:

- **DOM order**: keep DOM order equal to the design's visual right-to-left reading order — do NOT reverse the children yourself.
- **Icons next to text**: Figma may report an icon as "left of text" but in the rendered RTL layout that position is the **end** side. Judge leading/trailing by the design screenshot, not by the generated code's physical side.
- **Directional icons** (arrows, chevrons, "next"): flip only if the asset itself points the wrong way for RTL — never mirror generic icons.
- **Absolute centering** (`-translate-x-1/2 left-1/2`) is direction-neutral and stays as-is; directional x-axis translates may need flipping.
